# GitHub Environment: private-lxc (configure required reviewers before enabling).
# The repository had NO configured CI -> LXC route. These names describe required
# deployment inputs; they do not claim an existing reachable runner or tunnel.
# Existing operator SSH: root@192.168.0.164 from the trusted LAN workstation.
# Do NOT expose a public dashboard/control port to make CI work.
# Configure a genuinely reachable approved SSH route before executing CI deploy.
# GitHub environment VARIABLES (not automatically sourced by this example):
BUNS_SSH_HOST=
BUNS_SSH_USER=
BUNS_SSH_PORT=
# GitHub environment SECRETS (never paste values into tracked files):
BUNS_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Pre-approved known_hosts entry including correct hostname/[host]:port binding.
# Obtain the fingerprint through the existing trusted operator channel; CI never
# runs ssh-keyscan or disables StrictHostKeyChecking.
BUNS_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS=
# Host installation prerequisites, performed only after independent source gates:
# - root-owned /usr/local/sbin/buns-private-deploy from deployment/buns-private-deploy.sh
# - /etc/buns/assets.env + secret file, persistent shared dirs writable by gid1001
# - existing buns-web.service extended by its source template; buns-game-apply.service installed
# - Python >=3.11, aiohttp, compiler, zlib and liblz4 runtime for existing WZ tools
# - install the pinned checkout's tools/wz_release/requirements.txt into that Python
# - approved pinned WZ tools checkout and native/NX baseline manifests
# - assets.env NX_HTTP_ORIGIN selects the existing HTTP origin; consumer command
#   NX_CONSUMER_VERIFY_COMMAND runs /opt/buns/tools/verify_nx_consumer.py.
#   Install its genuine pinned-runtime probe prerequisites; no synthetic success.
# - publisher inputs at /opt/buns/publication-inputs/<approved-id>, operations.json
# - SSH principal allowed sudo -n ONLY the validating private-deploy command
# The WZ workflow checks host source HEAD == github.sha and waits actual common
# manifest commit. Its isolated CI tests do NOT claim genuine converter proof;
# that proof uses the explicit native/NX fixture and independent source gate.
